  "assumptions": [
    "Inherited core tally qualifications remain. This tally updates the explicit AIC2026 adapter; source_commit pins the inherited core analysis, and the adapter source is in the accompanying AIC refusal receipt.",
    "The AIC route calls the existing full-result API to obtain Q as well as Q_JOD; it also computes unused spatial maps. Added reconstruction uses the geometric-series upper bound for 13x13 upsample and 9x9 band taps plus 7x7/9x9 final taps. Boundary/zero-tap specialization is not counted exactly; this is an explicit upper logical-work estimate, not a measured operation total.",
    "The SDR EOTF is content-dependent. The stated count models the nonlinear branch for every component; dark-code components instead divide by 12.92. It is a logical upper-work model, not an instruction measurement.",
    "CLI route `--metric hdrvdp3` -> cpu_dispatch HDR -> hdrvdp3 score/hdrvdp3_run (v3/metric.rs:151-190). Default sweep path = score() (want_maps=false): skips pyramid reconstruct + s_map + P_map sweeps (metric.rs:445-460).",
    "v3 works in f64 throughout (fft64/trans64). Per image: ingress to nits (v3/ingress.rs), determine_pad, visual_pathway (v3/pathway.rs:98-350): cycdeg_image grid, MTF conv via fft64::conv_fft_pad_into on 2x-padded planes PER CHANNEL (pathway.rs:146-200, filter cached per dims), spectral aging optical-density filter (pathway.rs:217), photoreceptor-like transforms (trans64.rs), then Spyr0 pyramid (v3/spyr0.rs:601+).",
    "Spyr0 = isotropic Laplacian-style stack (spyr0.rs:4-22): hi0filt 9x9 stride-1 (spyr0.rs:254), lo0filt 7x7 stride-1 (spyr0.rs:201), per level bfilt 9x9 stride-1 (spyr0.rs:512) + lofilt 13x13 stride-2 (spyr0.rs:339). Direct 2-D corr_dn64, reflect1 padding, f64. band_count = levels+2; level dims ceil halving; levels ~ while min dim >=13 -> floor(log2(min/13))+1.",
    "Masking (metric.rs:386-470): per band-pair - band_diff (sub), for the BASE band an FFT2 dominant-frequency estimate (one fft64 per pair, metric.rs:400-415), ex_diff = sign_pow(diff,p) per el (trans64), apply_band division by (csf*(1+k*mask)) normaliser, masked sum fold -> q_err accumulate. csf_b built per band from log_la resample + CSF LUT lerp (256-entry).",
    "l_mean_adapt/log_la/diff_mask pointwise over W*H (metric.rs:322-340): mean of both l_adapt planes, log10, per-pixel any-channel diff flag ~3*channels ops.",
    "Per-band costs are f64; FFT conv is the only global-radius stage. Band-pair elements total ~ (1 + 1/4*(4/3)) * W*H ~ 1.33*W*H for oriented-level bands + hi0/lo0 residual at N -> ~2.4*W*H."
  ],
